cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this library, please cite it as below."
title: "OscInt: uniform oscillatory-integral estimates in Lean 4 and Mathlib"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + Mathlib library of machine-checked uniform oscillatory-integral estimates: van der Corput's lemma for
  every derivative order with explicit constants, non-stationary and nondegenerate stationary phase, uniform decay at
  fold (A2), cusp (A3) and umbilic (D4) points with the D4 leading term and its closed-form constant, global decay
  from a pointwise classification of the phase (also for amplitudes in any complex Banach space), front ends in
  Mathlib's idiom, and explicit bounds for the propagator kernel of the free discrete Schrödinger equation: on Z,
  |∫_{-π}^{π} e^{i(t cos k + ξk)} dk| ≤ 8(1 + √7)/3 · t^{-1/3} for all t > 0 and real ξ, and on Z^d the d-th power of
  that constant with t^{-d/3}. The degenerate-point and global bounds are uniform over all linear terms of the phase,
  as dispersive estimates need. Statements are frozen, timestamped and reviewed blind before their proofs (exceptions
  are disclosed), and the proofs are replayed by six kernel checkers; a downstream checker verifies that a project
  depends on exactly the reviewed statements. Proofs and reviews are largely by AI agents; statement fidelity has been
  reviewed by AI referees, not yet by a human expert.
